WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.552
Late in the afternoon one Christmas Eve, Ebenezer Scrooge and his clerk, Bob Cratchit, were hard at work.

2
00:00:07.553 --> 00:00:14.783
Ebenezer Scrooge was perhaps the cheapest, most cold-hearted, mean-spirited man that ever lived.

3
00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:23.633
He had no friends. On the street, not even the beggars would beg from him.

4
00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:29.760
Cratchit was a good and honest man, but working for Scrooge had kept his family poor.

5
00:00:29.761 --> 00:00:36.626
Cratchit was working as hard as he could, but it was difficult because Scrooge kept the office terribly cold.

6
00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:39.796
He was too cheap even to buy coal.

7
00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:45.303
Suddenly they heard a cheerful cry, "Merry Christmas, Uncle!"

8
00:00:45.304 --> 00:00:47.294
It was Scrooge's nephew.

9
00:00:47.295 --> 00:00:54.577
Being surprised, being interrupted, and hearing the words "Merry Christmas," all angered Scrooge.

10
00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:57.440
"Bah! Humbug!" he replied.

11
00:00:57.441 --> 00:01:01.275
"Christmas a humbug, Uncle?" His nephew laughed.

12
00:01:01.276 --> 00:01:05.926
"Christmas is for fools who waste their money," grunted Scrooge.

13
00:01:05.927 --> 00:01:09.141
"There is no profit."

14
00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:19.555
To this, his nephew replied, "Christmas is a time to remember the birth of Jesus, and to be kind, forgiving, loving, and pleasant to others.

15
00:01:19.556 --> 00:01:23.337
It is a time to know that all people are brothers and sisters.

16
00:01:23.338 --> 00:01:28.711
While it may not bring me profit, I say, 'God bless Christmas.'"

17
00:01:28.712 --> 00:01:31.765
"Bah! Humbug!" Scrooge replied.

18
00:01:31.766 --> 00:01:36.988
With a smile his nephew asked, "Would you at least come to dinner with us tomorrow?"

19
00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:41.593
"No, I will not. Now, good afternoon," snorted Scrooge.

20
00:01:41.594 --> 00:01:45.554
"Merry Christmas, Uncle," replied his nephew with a smile.

21
00:01:45.555 --> 00:01:51.898
With that, his nephew left, and two gentlemen walked in.

22
00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:58.336
"Mr. Scrooge, we are taking a Christmas collection for the poor," said one of the gentlemen.

23
00:01:58.337 --> 00:02:01.252
"Many have little or nothing to live on."

24
00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:06.817
To this, Scrooge replied, "Are there no prisons or workhouses?"

25
00:02:06.818 --> 00:02:16.091
"Mr. Scrooge! Most people would rather die than go to those terrible places," replied the gentlemen.

26
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:20.094
"If they would rather die, then fine," declared Scrooge.

27
00:02:20.095 --> 00:02:25.650
"Let them die. I will not waste my money on helping people who are lazy.

28
00:02:25.651 --> 00:02:31.503
Good afternoon, gentlemen." Shocked and disgusted, the men quickly left.

29
00:02:31.504 --> 00:02:38.881
Then, looking at his watch, Scrooge realized that it was time to close the office.

30
00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:43.865
"I guess you want tomorrow off," said Scrooge with a sigh.

31
00:02:43.866 --> 00:02:47.160
"It is Christmas, sir," replied Cratchit.

32
00:02:47.161 --> 00:02:51.813
"Bah! Humbug! It is a poor excuse," said Scrooge.

33
00:02:51.814 --> 00:02:57.471
"You'd better be here very early the next day."

34
00:02:57.472 --> 00:03:05.011
With that, the office was locked, and Scrooge went home to his dreary, lonely house.

35
00:03:05.012 --> 00:03:08.351
Scrooge once had a partner named Jacob Marley.

36
00:03:08.352 --> 00:03:13.199
But on Christmas Eve, seven years before, Marley had died.

37
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.337
Marley and Scrooge were similar in that they both had no friends, no family, and no hearts.

38
00:03:19.338 --> 00:03:27.266
Scrooge was the only one at Marley's funeral, and even he was not very sad.

39
00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:33.236
In fact, shortly after Marley died, Scrooge completely stopped thinking about him.

40
00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:38.163
That is why it was quite strange that, when Scrooge arrived at his house,

41
00:03:38.164 --> 00:03:45.501
the old knocker on his front door turned into the living face of Jacob Marley.

42
00:03:45.502 --> 00:03:49.344
Startled, Scrooge looked again and saw just a knocker.

43
00:03:49.345 --> 00:03:54.250
"Pooh! Pooh!" said Scrooge, thinking that he was acting silly.

44
00:03:54.251 --> 00:03:59.302
Without another thought, he entered and sat by a very low fire.

45
00:03:59.303 --> 00:04:08.113
Suddenly an old servant bell next to the fireplace began to ring loudly, giving Scrooge a shock.

46
00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:14.669
This was followed by a terrible noise, and then, through the locked door came a ghost.

47
00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.176
"What do you want?" declared Scrooge, trying to sound stern.

48
00:04:19.177 --> 00:04:21.712
"Much!" said the ghost.

49
00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:24.863
"Who are you?" asked Scrooge.

50
00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:32.877
"Who was I?" replied the ghost. "I was your partner, Jacob Marley.

51
00:04:32.878 --> 00:04:37.130
Listen carefully, Ebenezer," said Marley sternly.

52
00:04:37.131 --> 00:04:42.439
"In life, everyone must love others and help those in need.

53
00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:47.565
If not, after death, he is condemned to search the earth.

54
00:04:47.566 --> 00:04:56.016
I spent my entire life in our office counting money, and I never knew love or charity.

55
00:04:56.017 --> 00:05:04.351
Now I must wander the earth trying to make up for my selfish life, but it is too late.

56
00:05:04.352 --> 00:05:08.435
I see a poor woman with no food for her babies.

57
00:05:08.436 --> 00:05:12.267
I want to give her some money, but I can't.

58
00:05:12.268 --> 00:05:16.583
I must sit and watch her suffer."

59
00:05:16.584 --> 00:05:21.732
Scrooge began to shake with fear because he knew he was the same.

60
00:05:21.733 --> 00:05:26.853
"I am here tonight to help save you from my fate," said Marley.

61
00:05:26.854 --> 00:05:35.601
"Thank you," replied Scrooge. "You were always a good friend."

62
00:05:35.602 --> 00:05:39.847
"You will be haunted by three ghosts," said Marley.

63
00:05:39.848 --> 00:05:42.339
"They will come to you in your sleep."

64
00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:48.183
"Ghosts? I want no more ghosts," replied Scrooge.

65
00:05:48.184 --> 00:05:53.634
Marley repeated, "They are your only chance to escape my pain.

66
00:05:53.635 --> 00:05:59.236
The ghosts will come."

67
00:05:59.237 --> 00:06:02.058
With that, the ghost of Marley left.

68
00:06:02.059 --> 00:06:11.459
Exhausted from the terrible fright and not knowing what was true, Scrooge climbed into bed and went to sleep.

